{"ts": "2026-07-04T00:19:41.019Z", "seq": 3, "kind": "caveat", "summary": "DESIGN-ADDRESSED: the 0.8.14 Slice-0 ADR (dff4830c, D5) DISCHARGES this caveat — the D2 per-kind index-target set is the seam a later OPP-12 projection registry wraps; FTS/filter same-txn + vector async-via-worker preserved; terminal-cursor readiness kept per-kind-extensible. Now WATCHING: re-check the Slice-5 keystone actually honors the seam, and again at OPP-12 scheduling", "area": "engine/substrate", "epistemic": "verified", "id": "TC-1", "owner": "orchestrator", "priority": "p2", "status": "watching", "refs": ["seq:1", "git:dff4830c", "opp:OPP-12"], "body": "Advanced from open->watching. The ratified Slice-0 substrate ADR explicitly discharges TC-1 in §D5 (verified from git dff4830c): the engine already owns the async substrate a future OPP-12 projection registry needs (projection workers + _fathomdb_projection_terminal readiness = durable dense_readiness equivalent; per-kind kind_is_vector_indexed), and the ADR obligates EXP-S to (a) keep the D2 per-kind index-target set a wrappable seam, (b) preserve FTS/filter same-txn + vector async-via-worker (no collapse to sync), (c) keep terminal-cursor readiness per-kind-extensible. Trigger to re-check: the Slice-5 keystone implementation honors these; then close/re-open at OPP-12 scheduling (>=0.9.x)."}
{"ts": "2026-07-04T01:29:26.727Z", "seq": 4, "kind": "consideration", "summary": "Engine::bm25f_search scores by re-tokenizing each field via a temp-FTS5 round-trip (fts5_tokenize) per field/candidate — correctness-first, but there is NO perf gate on bm25f_search. A future perf pass / Slice 40 / the 1-2M scaling work should weigh this before F5 rides a hot path", "area": "engine/fts-bm25f", "epistemic": "verified", "id": "TC-3", "owner": "hitl", "priority": "p3", "status": "open", "refs": ["git:c57e4e99", "plan:dev/plans/plan-0.8.14.md"], "body": "Surfaced at 0.8.14 Slice 10 (F5 BM25F, c57e4e99); flagged by BOTH codex §9 and the implementer. The in-engine BM25F scorer (justified ADR-0.8.1 deviation — FTS5 bm25() pins k1/b, so scoring is done in-engine to honor R-F5-1's tunable b) computes per-field term stats by re-tokenizing each field through fts5_tokenize per field per candidate. Correct + tokenization-faithful (the fix-1 that resolved codex's medium finding), but O(fields x candidates) tokenizer round-trips with no perf gate on the path. Engine-internal / experimental today, so NOT blocking. Re-weigh before F5 is put on a hot/large query path: a perf gate at Slice 40 (release readiness) or during the 1-2M scaling work, or a caching/precompute optimization. Ref c57e4e99 (bm25f_search)."}
{"ts": "2026-07-05T20:13:03.419Z", "seq": 5, "kind": "todo", "summary": "ENFORCE the HITL mandate in tooling: the eu7/eval harness + eval runners MUST DEFAULT to GPU embedding (embed-cuda + FATHOMDB_EMBED_DEVICE=cuda:0, rerank-cuda for rerank) when the 3090s have compute+memory room, CPU fallback only -- so no agent has to remember the flags. Exclude the K620 (FATHOMDB_GPU_EXCLUDE); check nvidia-smi room before dispatch; verify GPU engaged", "area": "eval/gpu", "epistemic": "verified", "id": "TC-4", "owner": "hitl", "priority": "p1", "status": "open", "refs": ["file:dev/design/gpu-eval-activities-policy.md", "opp:none"], "body": "Standing HITL mandate 2026-07-05 (policy: dev/design/gpu-eval-activities-policy.md; memory repo-must-use-gpu-for-eval-when-3090-room). Root cause: a fresh 0.8.14 eu7 run crawled on the CPU embedder (~0.43 docs/sec, seed-timeout-prone) with both 3090s at 0% idle. GPU is 15-93x faster (0.8.7) and CPU<->CUDA is 1-bit identical (fidelity-safe). Per fix-the-tooling-not-people: make GPU-when-room the DEFAULT in the eu7 harness (eu7_real_corpus_ac.rs currently builds --features default-embedder = CPU) + the eval runners (agent-build.sh / eval scripts), with a room-check (nvidia-smi util+free-mem) and CPU fallback only when the 3090s are busy/full. Watch the GPU-eval build traps (libcuda bundling / stale .so shadowing, eval-environment-operational-notes). SCOPE: internal eval/dev/CI only; shipped-library default (CPU/opt-in) unchanged. PLACEMENT TBD (HITL): fold into 0.8.14 Slice 40, or a fast-follow pico. Interim: pass the env/flags explicitly per run (the current eu7 re-run already switched to GPU)."}
{"ts": "2026-07-05T20:16:50.031Z", "seq": 6, "kind": "todo", "summary": "REFINED (HITL 2025-07-05): CPU is NOT a general fallback. Full eval/embed/rerank suites ALWAYS run on GPU; CPU is permitted ONLY for two narrow probes -- (1) simple CPU-compatibility testing, (2) CPU-library repeatability/compatibility checks. 'Feature compatibility' = check compat with CPU libraries, NOT run full suites on both CPU+GPU. When 3090s busy: wait/queue or use the other 3090, never a full CPU run. Harness/eval-runner default = GPU for full runs", "area": "eval/gpu", "epistemic": "verified", "id": "TC-4", "owner": "hitl", "priority": "p1", "status": "open", "refs": ["seq:5", "file:dev/design/gpu-eval-activities-policy.md"], "body": "Tightens the enforcement scope. The eu7/eval harness + eval runners MUST default to GPU for full runs; there is NO CPU full-suite fallback. CPU is reserved for minimal, targeted compatibility probes only: a CPU-code-path build/run smoke, and a CPU-library repeatability/compatibility check -- never a mirror of the full GPU suite. On a busy GPU, wait/queue or use cuda:1, don't run the full suite on CPU. Policy: dev/design/gpu-eval-activities-policy.md (updated). Placement of the tooling change still TBD (HITL): 0.8.14 Slice 40 or a fast-follow pico."}
{"ts": "2026-07-06T01:25:40.538Z", "seq": 7, "kind": "todo", "summary": "Re-baseline the eu7 0.90 recall floor for the GROWN 18,472-doc cross-source corpus. The floor + the 0.896 CPU baseline (ci_hi 0.925) predate the musique (Jun 16) + compmix (Jul 3) cross-source additions, which mechanically lower recall@10 at fixed N. Needs a fresh CPU same-backend eu7 N=7667 measurement on the current corpus + an HITL threshold ruling on a corpus-appropriate floor. Separate from 0.8.14 (D6 zero vec0 rewrite excludes a regression)", "area": "eval/eu7", "epistemic": "verified", "id": "TC-5", "owner": "hitl", "priority": "p1", "status": "open", "refs": ["file:dev/design/gpu-eval-activities-policy.md", "plan:dev/plans/plan-0.8.14.md"], "body": "Surfaced at 0.8.14 Slice 20: a GPU eu7 run read vector-stage recall@10 N=7667=0.833 (ci_hi 0.864 < 0.90) vs the historical CPU baseline 0.896 (ci_hi 0.925 PASS); N=1000=0.950 PASS. Two verified confounds: (1) cross-backend (GPU embed vs CPU baseline; near-threshold 1-bit-quant flips at large N) -- fixed forward: eu7/fidelity gates now run CPU same-backend per gpu-eval-activities-policy.md; (2) corpus growth (musique+compmix added post-baseline). D6 (codex-verified zero vec0 rewrite @ Slice 5) excludes a 0.8.14 regression, so Slice 20 closed on the D6 no-op basis (HITL). OPEN: is 0.90 still right for the grown corpus? Resolve via a fresh CPU same-backend eu7 N=7667 on the current corpus, then an HITL floor ruling (keep 0.90 or re-baseline). Placement TBD."}
