{"ts": "2026-07-09T12:27:12.326Z", "seq": 18, "kind": "todo", "summary": "TC-9 EXTENSION (D3/L3 finding, 2026-07-09, Steward-verified): ONNX-GPU-EP cross-backend Delta measured OOB (durable doc git:76568975). candle-CPU(Cls) <-> ONNX-CUDA-EP(Cls; ORT 1.26.0 GPU + cuDNN 9.5 + RTX3090 cuda:1) = 2/17280 raw sign flips (1/17280 proxy-mean-centered), cosine 0.99999996, L2 <= 5.4e-4, deterministic x3, EFFECTIVE PROVIDER VERIFIED CUDA -- the FIRST non-byte-identical cross-backend leg (both prior CPU legs = 0 flips; pure GPU FP divergence, not a broken export). FINDING: as-shipped OrtBgeEmbedder under ort=2.0.0-rc.10 (default-features=false) CANNOT instantiate the CUDA EP -- ort::init() is never called (Steward-verified ABSENT in ort_bge.rs; the EP-dispatch + loud-fallback code IS present) -> ORT 'DefaultLogger not registered' -> LOUD CPU fallback. Proven binding-not-host: same native stack runs CUDA via Python + via a standalone rc.10 probe WITH a one-time ort::init().commit(). NOT a shipped hazard (ONNX = opt-in non-default EVAL feature; fallback is LOUD not silent; default library path = candle-CPU, unaffected). ACTION folded into TC-9 (ort 2.0-stable bump): (a) add a one-time ORT env init so ONNX GPU/cross-vendor EPs are reachable, (b) re-verify CUDA-EP session creation on 2.0-stable. #5/D4 BEARING: none now -- the D4 same-identity floor stays tight (0 flips; same-identity candle CPU<->CUDA was 0/6144 @0.8.7), and the 2-flip GPU-EP leg is a DISTINCT '-onnx' identity already refused by identity + R-VEQ-5 additive-only; a FUTURE cross-vendor portability ADR must budget a NON-ZERO GPU-EP flip rate.", "decider": "steward", "extends": "TC-9", "refs": ["git:76568975", "file:dev/plans/runs/0.8.18-slice-0-onnx-gpu-ep-calibration.md", "file:src/rust/crates/fathomdb-embedder/src/ort_bge.rs"]}
